1
00:00:01,293 --> 00:00:02,586
WE WENT TO THE BEACH.

2
00:00:02,628 --> 00:00:04,546
PHOEBE FOUND THIS LADY
WHO KNEW HER PARENTS.

3
00:00:04,588 --> 00:00:06,423
I DON'T KNOW
WHAT HAPPENED WITH THAT.

4
00:00:06,465 --> 00:00:08,258
I'M YOUR MOTHER.

5
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:09,593
HUH?

6
00:00:09,635 --> 00:00:11,094
MONICA JOKED SHE WOULDN'T

7
00:00:11,136 --> 00:00:12,930
GO OUT WITH
A GUY LIKE CHANDLER.

8
00:00:12,972 --> 00:00:14,431
HE COULDN'T LET IT GO.

9
00:00:14,473 --> 00:00:16,015
I DON'T KNOW
WHAT HAPPENED WITH THAT.

10
00:00:16,057 --> 00:00:18,393
THEN ROSS'S NEW GIRLFRIEND,
BONNIE, SHOWS UP

11
00:00:18,435 --> 00:00:20,896
AND RACHEL CONVINCED HER
TO SHAVE HER HEAD.

12
00:00:20,938 --> 00:00:22,523
THEN ROSS AND RACHEL KISS.

13
00:00:22,564 --> 00:00:24,316
ROSS HAS TO CHOOSE
BETWEEN RACHEL

14
00:00:24,358 --> 00:00:25,901
AND THE BALD GIRL...

15
00:00:25,943 --> 00:00:28,904
AND I DON'T KNOW WHAT HAPPENED
THERE, EITHER.

16
00:00:28,946 --> 00:00:30,698
LET ME GO GET CHANDLER.

17
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:44,252
HI.

18
00:00:44,294 --> 00:00:45,587
HEY.
HI.

19
00:00:45,629 --> 00:00:48,465
RACHEL WAS JUST
HELPING ME OUT.

20
00:00:48,507 --> 00:00:50,759
MY HEAD GOT
ALL SUNBURNED.

21
00:00:50,801 --> 00:00:52,803
AW.

22
00:00:52,845 --> 00:00:54,346
THANKS A MILLION.

23
00:00:54,388 --> 00:00:56,974
OH, YOU'RE WELCOME
A MILLION.

24
00:00:57,016 --> 00:00:58,726
OKAY, I'LL BE
IN OUR ROOM.

25
00:01:11,655 --> 00:01:13,574
OH, MY GOD.

26
00:01:13,615 --> 00:01:14,867
I KNOW.

27
00:01:18,996 --> 00:01:20,455
OKAY, I GOT TO GO.

28
00:01:20,497 --> 00:01:21,916
WHAT? WHAT?

29
00:01:21,957 --> 00:01:24,960
I GOT TO GO
BREAK UP WITH BONNIE.

30
00:01:25,002 --> 00:01:27,128
HERE? NOW?

31
00:01:27,170 --> 00:01:28,463
WELL, YEAH.

32
00:01:28,505 --> 00:01:30,131
I CAN'T STAY HERE
ALL NIGHT.

33
00:01:30,173 --> 00:01:32,676
IF I GO IN THERE,
SHE'LL WANT TO...

34
00:01:32,718 --> 00:01:34,011
DO STUFF.

35
00:01:34,053 --> 00:01:35,679
CAN'T YOU JUST TELL HER

36
00:01:35,721 --> 00:01:37,848
THAT YOU ARE NOT IN THE MOOD?

37
00:01:37,890 --> 00:01:41,351
NO, SHE LIKES THAT.

38
00:01:41,393 --> 00:01:43,353
FAKING SLEEP
DOESN'T WORK, EITHER.

39
00:01:43,395 --> 00:01:44,980
I CAN'T TELL YOU HOW MANY
MORNINGS I WOKE UP WITH HER...

40
00:01:45,022 --> 00:01:46,189
EW.

41
00:01:46,231 --> 00:01:47,524
OKAY.

42
00:01:47,566 --> 00:01:50,110
WHY AM I TELLING
YOU THAT?

43
00:01:50,151 --> 00:01:52,362
I DON'T KNOW.

44
00:01:58,744 --> 00:01:59,954
UH...

45
00:01:59,995 --> 00:02:02,163
IT WASN'T EVERY MORNING...

46
00:02:02,205 --> 00:02:03,206
MAKING IT WORSE.

47
00:02:03,248 --> 00:02:04,249
OKAY.

48
00:02:10,965 --> 00:02:15,385
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

49
00:02:15,427 --> 00:02:17,763
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

50
00:02:17,805 --> 00:02:20,432
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

51
00:02:20,474 --> 00:02:25,312
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

52
00:02:25,353 --> 00:02:26,814
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN YOUR DAY ♪

53
00:02:26,855 --> 00:02:30,109
♪ YOUR WEEK, YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

54
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:33,946
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

55
00:02:33,988 --> 00:02:36,197
♪ WHEN THE RAIN
STARTS TO POUR ♪

56
00:02:36,239 --> 00:02:38,867
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

57
00:02:38,909 --> 00:02:41,120
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

58
00:02:41,161 --> 00:02:43,664
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

59
00:02:43,705 --> 00:02:47,793
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME TOO. ♪

60
00:02:55,134 --> 00:02:58,345
I GUESS YOU'D LIKE
TO KNOW HOW IT ALL HAPPENED.

61
00:02:58,386 --> 00:03:00,555
I-I MEAN, I THINK
I CAN FIGURE IT OUT.

62
00:03:00,597 --> 00:03:01,974
I GUESS I WAS BORN

63
00:03:02,016 --> 00:03:04,559
AND THEN, EVERYONE STARTED
LYING THEIR ASSES OFF.

64
00:03:04,601 --> 00:03:06,687
NO, NO.
IT WASN'T LIKE THAT.

65
00:03:06,728 --> 00:03:10,189
REMEMBER HOW I TOLD YOU
HOW LILY AND FRANK AND I

66
00:03:10,231 --> 00:03:11,525
WERE CLOSE?

67
00:03:11,566 --> 00:03:14,444
WELL, WE WERE VERY CLOSE.

68
00:03:14,486 --> 00:03:16,071
HOW CLOSE?

69
00:03:16,113 --> 00:03:18,115
WELL, THE THREE OF US

70
00:03:18,157 --> 00:03:20,450
WE WERE KIND OF A COUPLE.

71
00:03:20,492 --> 00:03:23,244
I DON'T EVEN KNOW HOW
THAT WOULD WORK.

72
00:03:23,286 --> 00:03:24,121
WELL, WE WOULD...

73
00:03:24,163 --> 00:03:25,413
I'M NOT ASKING.

74
00:03:25,455 --> 00:03:29,376
WELL, ANYHOW,
SOMEHOW, I GOT PREGNANT

75
00:03:29,417 --> 00:03:31,586
AND I WAS...

76
00:03:31,628 --> 00:03:32,713
SCARED.

77
00:03:32,754 --> 00:03:34,589
I WAS STUPID AND SELFISH AND...

78
00:03:34,631 --> 00:03:35,883
I WAS 18 YEARS OLD.

79
00:03:35,924 --> 00:03:38,052
I MEAN, YOU REMEMBER
WHAT IT WAS LIKE

80
00:03:38,093 --> 00:03:39,887
TO BE 18 YEARS OLD, DON'T YOU?

81
00:03:39,928 --> 00:03:40,888
YEAH.

82
00:03:40,929 --> 00:03:42,305
LET'S SEE...

83
00:03:42,347 --> 00:03:45,017
MY MOM HAD KILLED HERSELF
AND MY DAD HAD RUN OFF

84
00:03:45,059 --> 00:03:48,062
AND I WAS LIVING IN A GREMLIN
WITH A GUY NAMED CINDY

85
00:03:48,103 --> 00:03:49,813
WHO TALKED
TO HIS HAND.

86
00:03:49,855 --> 00:03:51,148
OH, I'M SO SORRY.

87
00:03:51,190 --> 00:03:52,733
I THOUGHT I WAS LEAVING YOU

88
00:03:52,774 --> 00:03:54,735
WITH THE BEST PARENTS
IN THE WORLD.

89
00:03:54,776 --> 00:03:56,904
I DIDN'T EVEN HEAR
ABOUT YOUR MOM AND DAD

90
00:03:56,945 --> 00:03:58,405
TILL A COUPLE
OF YEARS AGO.

91
00:03:58,446 --> 00:04:00,199
BY THEN, YOU WERE
ALREADY GROWN UP

92
00:04:00,239 --> 00:04:01,783
AND, I DON'T KNOW,
YOU'RE HERE

93
00:04:01,825 --> 00:04:03,118
AND I WOULD REALLY...

94
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:04,953
I WOULD LIKE
TO GET TO KNOW YOU.

95
00:04:04,995 --> 00:04:06,955
YEAH, WELL, EVERYBODY DOES.

96
00:04:06,997 --> 00:04:08,916
I'M A REALLY COOL PERSON.

97
00:04:08,957 --> 00:04:12,586
AND, YOU KNOW, YOU HAD
29 YEARS TO FIND THAT OUT

98
00:04:12,627 --> 00:04:14,504
BUT YOU DIDN'T EVEN TRY.

99
00:04:14,546 --> 00:04:16,381
YOU KNOW WHAT?

100
00:04:16,423 --> 00:04:17,465
YOU WALKED OUT ON ME.

101
00:04:17,507 --> 00:04:18,926
I'M DOING THE SAME TO YOU.

102
00:04:18,967 --> 00:04:20,135
WAIT...

103
00:04:20,177 --> 00:04:23,597
I DON'T EVER WANT
TO SEE YOU AGAIN.

104
00:04:23,638 --> 00:04:25,724
( sighs )

105
00:04:25,766 --> 00:04:27,475
WHERE'S MY PURSE?

106
00:04:29,853 --> 00:04:31,730
SHOOT. WE'RE OUT
OF SODA.

107
00:04:31,772 --> 00:04:33,648
I'LL GO OUT
AND GET YOU SOME.

108
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:34,816
REALLY?

109
00:04:34,858 --> 00:04:37,402
NOPE, 'CAUSE I'M NOT
YOUR BOYFRIEND.

110
00:04:39,029 --> 00:04:41,489
HEY, PHEEBS,
HOW DID IT GO?

111
00:04:41,531 --> 00:04:43,700
WELL...

112
00:04:43,742 --> 00:04:45,452
MY MOM'S FRIEND, PHOEBE

113
00:04:45,493 --> 00:04:47,328
IS ACTUALLY MY BIRTH MOM.

114
00:04:50,082 --> 00:04:53,127
I FOUND A DRIED-UP SEA HORSE.

115
00:04:53,168 --> 00:04:55,462
SWEETIE,
WHAT ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT?

116
00:04:55,503 --> 00:04:56,797
OH, MY NEW MOM

117
00:04:56,838 --> 00:04:58,715
WHO'S A BIG, FAT ABANDONER.

118
00:04:58,757 --> 00:05:00,467
WELL, PHEEBS,
WAIT A SECOND.

119
00:05:00,508 --> 00:05:03,386
DON'T YOU WANT TO STAY HERE
AND TALK ABOUT IT?

120
00:05:03,428 --> 00:05:04,930
NO. I WANT...

121
00:05:04,972 --> 00:05:07,141
I NEED
TO BE ALONE.

122
00:05:10,227 --> 00:05:11,019
MONICA?!

123
00:05:11,061 --> 00:05:12,395
OH.

124
00:05:21,696 --> 00:05:22,990
IT'S OVER.

125
00:05:23,031 --> 00:05:26,118
OH, WAS IT AWFUL?

126
00:05:26,160 --> 00:05:28,245
WELL, IT WAS LONG.

127
00:05:28,287 --> 00:05:30,622
I DIDN'T EVEN REALIZE
HOW LATE IT WAS

128
00:05:30,664 --> 00:05:32,124
TILL I NOTICED
THE 5:00 SHADOW

129
00:05:32,166 --> 00:05:34,459
ON HER HEAD.

130
00:05:34,501 --> 00:05:35,836
( stifled laugh )

131
00:05:38,337 --> 00:05:40,757
ANYWAY, SHE DIDN'T
WANT TO STAY.

132
00:05:40,799 --> 00:05:42,092
I CALLED A CAB.

133
00:05:42,134 --> 00:05:43,468
SHE JUST LEFT.

134
00:05:50,684 --> 00:05:52,644
I WROTE YOU A LETTER.

135
00:05:52,686 --> 00:05:54,646
OH, THANK YOU.

136
00:05:55,856 --> 00:05:57,941
I LIKE MAIL.

137
00:06:01,903 --> 00:06:03,280
THERE'S JUST...

138
00:06:03,322 --> 00:06:05,657
YOU KNOW, SOME THINGS
I'VE BEEN THINKING ABOUT--

139
00:06:05,699 --> 00:06:07,242
THINGS ABOUT US--

140
00:06:07,284 --> 00:06:08,285
AND BEFORE
I CAN EVEN THINK ABOUT

141
00:06:08,327 --> 00:06:09,703
THE TWO OF US
GETTING BACK TOGETHER

142
00:06:09,744 --> 00:06:12,080
I JUST NEED TO KNOW
HOW YOU FEEL

143
00:06:12,122 --> 00:06:13,957
ABOUT THIS STUFF.

144
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:17,127
OKAY.

145
00:06:17,169 --> 00:06:18,586
OKAY.

146
00:06:22,132 --> 00:06:23,800
IT'S...

147
00:06:23,842 --> 00:06:26,136
IT'S 5:30 IN THE MORNING.

148
00:06:29,056 --> 00:06:33,476
SO... I BETTER GET
CRACKING ON THIS BABY.

149
00:06:33,518 --> 00:06:35,436
SO, I'LL BE WAITING FOR YOU.

150
00:06:35,478 --> 00:06:37,564
JUST COME UP WHEN YOU'RE DONE.

151
00:06:37,605 --> 00:06:38,940
OKAY.

152
00:06:38,982 --> 00:06:41,526
I'LL BE UP IN...

153
00:06:41,568 --> 00:06:43,028
18 PAGES.

154
00:06:45,113 --> 00:06:46,447
FRONT AND BACK.

155
00:06:48,116 --> 00:06:49,993
IT'S VERY EXCITING.

156
00:07:07,010 --> 00:07:08,762
OH, OH, OH.

157
00:07:14,309 --> 00:07:15,810
HEY.

158
00:07:15,852 --> 00:07:17,145
WHAT HAPPENED TO YOU?

159
00:07:17,187 --> 00:07:18,605
WHY DIDN'T YOU
COME UP?

160
00:07:18,646 --> 00:07:20,023
DONE.

161
00:07:21,775 --> 00:07:23,151
YOU JUST FINISHED?

162
00:07:23,193 --> 00:07:25,528
WELL, I WANTED
TO BE THOROUGH.

163
00:07:25,570 --> 00:07:27,822
I MEAN, THIS IS CLEARLY

164
00:07:27,864 --> 00:07:30,075
VERY, VERY IMPORTANT
TO YOU...

165
00:07:30,117 --> 00:07:31,410
TO US.

166
00:07:31,450 --> 00:07:35,455
SO I WANTED TO READ
EVERY WORD CAREFULLY...

167
00:07:35,496 --> 00:07:36,539
TWICE.

168
00:07:38,166 --> 00:07:39,667
SO, UM...

169
00:07:41,002 --> 00:07:42,421
DOES IT?

170
00:07:48,051 --> 00:07:49,344
I'M SORRY?

171
00:07:51,679 --> 00:07:53,223
DOES IT?

172
00:07:53,265 --> 00:07:55,183
DOES IT?

173
00:07:56,184 --> 00:07:57,811
DOES IT?

174
00:08:00,563 --> 00:08:04,276
YEAH, I WANTED TO GIVE
THAT WHOLE "DOES IT" PART

175
00:08:04,318 --> 00:08:05,902
JUST ANOTHER GLANCE.

176
00:08:05,944 --> 00:08:07,486
WHAT ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT?

177
00:08:07,528 --> 00:08:09,281
YOU SAID
YOU READ IT TWICE.

178
00:08:09,323 --> 00:08:11,158
LOOK, IT EITHER
DOES OR IT DOESN'T

179
00:08:11,199 --> 00:08:13,368
AND IF YOU HAVE
TO EVEN THINK ABOUT IT...

180
00:08:13,410 --> 00:08:14,744
NO, NO, RACH,
NO, I DON'T.

181
00:08:14,786 --> 00:08:17,080
I DON'T HAVE TO THINK
ABOUT IT. I DON'T.

182
00:08:17,122 --> 00:08:18,081
IN FACT...

183
00:08:18,123 --> 00:08:19,582
I'VE DECIDED.

184
00:08:19,624 --> 00:08:22,002
I HAVE DECIDED THAT...

185
00:08:22,043 --> 00:08:23,378
THAT IT...

186
00:08:29,217 --> 00:08:30,635
DOES.

187
00:08:32,262 --> 00:08:33,805
( sniffling )

188
00:08:47,235 --> 00:08:48,236
ARE YOU SURE?

189
00:08:48,278 --> 00:08:50,280
SURE, I'M SURE.

190
00:08:56,328 --> 00:08:58,872
ALL RIGHT, THERE'S
A NUCLEAR HOLOCAUST.

191
00:08:58,913 --> 00:09:01,666
I'M THE LAST MAN ON EARTH.

192
00:09:01,708 --> 00:09:03,210
WOULD YOU GO OUT WITH ME?

193
00:09:04,919 --> 00:09:06,380
EHH.

194
00:09:09,216 --> 00:09:10,884
I'VE GOT CANNED GOODS.

195
00:09:12,386 --> 00:09:14,971
HEY, GUYS, TAKE A LOOK
AT THIS.

196
00:09:15,013 --> 00:09:16,764
CHECK THIS BABY OUT.

197
00:09:16,806 --> 00:09:18,641
DUG ME A HOLE.

198
00:09:20,643 --> 00:09:23,063
EXCELLENT HOLE, JOE.

199
00:09:24,105 --> 00:09:25,315
OH, NO!

200
00:09:25,357 --> 00:09:26,649
MY HOLE!

201
00:09:26,691 --> 00:09:28,902
OW! OW!

202
00:09:28,943 --> 00:09:30,529
WHAT IS IT?

203
00:09:30,569 --> 00:09:31,779
JELLYFISH STING!

204
00:09:31,821 --> 00:09:33,156
IT HURTS! IT HURTS!

205
00:09:33,198 --> 00:09:34,449
CAN WE HELP YOU?

206
00:09:34,491 --> 00:09:36,535
YOU WANT US TO TAKE YOU
BACK TO THE HOUSE?

207
00:09:36,576 --> 00:09:37,869
IT'S LIKE TWO MILES.

208
00:09:37,911 --> 00:09:40,288
AND I'M A LITTLE TIRED
FROM DIGGING THE HOLE.

209
00:09:40,330 --> 00:09:41,373
OW! OW!

210
00:09:41,415 --> 00:09:43,333
DAMN THE JELLYFISH!

211
00:09:43,375 --> 00:09:46,044
DAMN ALL THE JELLYFISH!

212
00:09:46,086 --> 00:09:47,795
WE'VE GOT
TO DO SOMETHING.

213
00:09:47,837 --> 00:09:49,548
THERE'S ONLY ONE THING
YOU CAN DO.

214
00:09:49,589 --> 00:09:50,840
WHAT? WHAT IS IT?

215
00:09:50,882 --> 00:09:52,300
YOU HAVE TO PEE ON IT.

216
00:09:52,342 --> 00:09:53,634
WHAT?!

217
00:09:53,676 --> 00:09:54,802
GROSS!

218
00:09:54,844 --> 00:09:56,137
DON'T BLAME ME.

219
00:09:56,179 --> 00:09:58,557
I SAW IT
ON THE DISCOVERY CHANNEL.

220
00:09:58,598 --> 00:10:00,183
YOU KNOW WHAT?
HE'S RIGHT.

221
00:10:00,225 --> 00:10:02,561
THERE'S SOMETHING
LIKE AMMONIA IN THAT

222
00:10:02,602 --> 00:10:03,895
THAT KILLS THE PAIN.

223
00:10:03,937 --> 00:10:05,230
WELL, FORGET IT.

224
00:10:05,272 --> 00:10:06,856
IT DOESN'T HURT THAT...

225
00:10:06,898 --> 00:10:08,442
BAD!

226
00:10:08,483 --> 00:10:11,528
IF YOU WANT SOME PRIVACY,
YOU CAN USE MY HOLE.

227
00:10:14,281 --> 00:10:18,034
WELL, I'M READY
TO GET THE HELL OUT OF HERE.

228
00:10:19,244 --> 00:10:20,287
OH...

229
00:10:20,328 --> 00:10:21,871
ARE YOU..?

230
00:10:21,913 --> 00:10:22,872
ARE YOU?!

231
00:10:22,914 --> 00:10:25,500
OH, THAT'S SO GREAT!

232
00:10:25,542 --> 00:10:26,960
OOH, NOT FOR BONNIE.

233
00:10:28,795 --> 00:10:32,048
BUT FOR YOU, YAY.

234
00:10:32,090 --> 00:10:32,882
HEY.

235
00:10:32,924 --> 00:10:34,092
Rachel:
HOW WAS THE BEACH?

236
00:10:34,134 --> 00:10:35,843
NOTHING. I DON'T KNOW.
( mumbling )

237
00:10:37,678 --> 00:10:39,097
WHAT
HAPPENED?

238
00:10:39,139 --> 00:10:40,432
NOTHING.

239
00:10:40,474 --> 00:10:42,350
I'M GOING TO TAKE
A SHOWER.

240
00:10:42,392 --> 00:10:43,684
ME, TOO.

241
00:10:43,726 --> 00:10:45,270
ME, TOO.

242
00:10:45,312 --> 00:10:48,189
OKAY, I'M GOING TO PUT
THIS IN THE CAR.

243
00:10:48,231 --> 00:10:49,816
OH, I HAVE
TO GO PACK.

244
00:10:49,857 --> 00:10:51,276
OH.

245
00:10:51,318 --> 00:10:52,777
AND IT REALLY DOES?

246
00:10:52,819 --> 00:10:54,112
IT DOES.

247
00:10:54,154 --> 00:10:56,364
IT REALLY AND TRULY DOES.

248
00:11:18,970 --> 00:11:22,723
IT SO DOES NOT!

249
00:11:27,812 --> 00:11:29,772
SHE WANTS ME
TO TAKE RESPONSIBILITY

250
00:11:29,814 --> 00:11:32,567
FOR EVERYTHING THAT WENT WRONG
IN OUR RELATIONSHIP.

251
00:11:32,609 --> 00:11:34,986
I MEAN, SHE GOES ON
FOR FIVE PAGES

252
00:11:35,028 --> 00:11:38,657
ABOUT HOW I WAS
UNFAITHFUL TO HER.

253
00:11:38,697 --> 00:11:41,451
WE WERE ON A BREAK!

254
00:11:41,493 --> 00:11:43,953
OH, MY GOD!
IF YOU SAY THAT ONE MORE TIME

255
00:11:43,995 --> 00:11:45,746
I'LL BREAK UP WITH YOU.

256
00:11:45,788 --> 00:11:49,334
FINE, FINE. BUT THIS BREAKUP
WAS NOT ALL MY FAULT

257
00:11:49,376 --> 00:11:51,044
AND SHE SAYS HERE

258
00:11:51,085 --> 00:11:53,129
"IF YOU ACCEPT FULL
RESPONSIBILITY..."

259
00:11:53,171 --> 00:11:54,631
FULL RESPONSIBILITY!

260
00:11:54,673 --> 00:11:56,675
"I CAN BEGIN TO TRUST YOU AGAIN.

261
00:11:56,715 --> 00:11:59,135
"DOES THAT SEEM LIKE
SOMETHING YOU CAN DO?

262
00:11:59,177 --> 00:12:00,595
DOES IT?!"

263
00:12:02,681 --> 00:12:04,015
NO?

264
00:12:05,766 --> 00:12:08,102
YOU HAVE WHAT YOU WANT.

265
00:12:08,144 --> 00:12:09,312
YOU'RE BACK WITH RACHEL.

266
00:12:09,354 --> 00:12:10,689
IF YOU BRING THIS UP NOW

267
00:12:10,771 --> 00:12:12,440
YOU'LL WRECK THE BEST THING
THAT EVER HAPPENED TO YOU.

268
00:12:12,482 --> 00:12:14,025
YEAH, I KNOW.

269
00:12:14,067 --> 00:12:15,485
YOU'RE RIGHT.

270
00:12:15,527 --> 00:12:16,570
( sighs )

271
00:12:16,611 --> 00:12:18,572
YEAH, I GUESS
I'LL LET IT GO.

272
00:12:18,613 --> 00:12:20,114
BUT YOU... YOU UNDERSTAND

273
00:12:20,156 --> 00:12:22,283
HOW HARD IT IS
TO FORGET ABOUT THIS.

274
00:12:22,325 --> 00:12:23,868
SURE, IT'S HARD
TO FORGET

275
00:12:23,910 --> 00:12:26,913
BUT THAT DOESN'T MEAN YOU
HAVE TO TALK ABOUT IT.

276
00:12:26,954 --> 00:12:29,499
A LOT OF THINGS HAPPENED
ON THAT TRIP

277
00:12:29,541 --> 00:12:32,960
THAT WE SHOULD NEVER,
EVER TALK ABOUT.

278
00:12:35,714 --> 00:12:38,299
WHAT THE HELL HAPPENED
ON THAT BEACH?

279
00:12:39,342 --> 00:12:42,970
IT'S BETWEEN US
AND THE SEA, ROSS.

280
00:12:52,105 --> 00:12:53,314
HI, URSULA.

281
00:12:53,356 --> 00:12:54,315
HEY.

282
00:12:54,357 --> 00:12:55,650
OKAY, WELL, I KNOW

283
00:12:55,692 --> 00:12:58,027
THAT WE HAVEN'T TALKED
IN A LONG TIME

284
00:12:58,069 --> 00:12:59,070
BUT, UM, OKAY...

285
00:12:59,112 --> 00:13:01,531
OUR MOM IS NOT OUR BIRTH MOM.

286
00:13:01,573 --> 00:13:04,033
THIS OTHER LADY
IS OUR BIRTH MOM.

287
00:13:04,075 --> 00:13:07,328
RIGHT. OKAY. THE ONE THAT
LIVES IN MONTAUK. MM-HMM.

288
00:13:07,370 --> 00:13:08,913
YOU KNOW HER?

289
00:13:08,955 --> 00:13:12,875
NO. I, UM, I READ ABOUT HER
IN MOM'S SUICIDE NOTE.

290
00:13:12,917 --> 00:13:15,044
THERE WAS A SUICIDE NOTE?

291
00:13:15,086 --> 00:13:17,422
WELL, DO YOU STILL HAVE IT?

292
00:13:18,423 --> 00:13:19,507
HANG ON.

293
00:13:22,051 --> 00:13:23,970
I CAN'T BELIEVE
YOU DIDN'T TELL ME

294
00:13:24,011 --> 00:13:25,680
THERE WAS A SUICIDE NOTE.

295
00:13:25,722 --> 00:13:27,890
YEAH. SO HOW HAVE
YOU BEEN DOING?

296
00:13:27,932 --> 00:13:30,268
I'VE... UH... SHUT UP.

297
00:13:34,147 --> 00:13:36,023
"GOOD-BYE, PHOEBE AND URSULA.

298
00:13:36,065 --> 00:13:37,317
"I'LL MISS YOU.

299
00:13:37,358 --> 00:13:39,902
P.S. YOUR MOM
LIVES IN MONTAUK."

300
00:13:41,237 --> 00:13:42,947
YOU JUST WROTE THIS!

301
00:13:43,948 --> 00:13:46,660
WELL, IT'S PRETTY
MUCH THE GIST.

302
00:13:47,661 --> 00:13:49,496
WELL, EXCEPT FOR THE POEM.

303
00:13:49,537 --> 00:13:51,414
YOU READ THE POEM, RIGHT?

304
00:13:51,456 --> 00:13:53,500
NO.

305
00:13:53,541 --> 00:13:55,293
ALL RIGHT. HANG ON.

306
00:14:00,381 --> 00:14:03,301
PASS THE CHEESE, PLEASE.

307
00:14:04,719 --> 00:14:06,387
( groans )

308
00:14:07,972 --> 00:14:10,684
MY GOD, YOU CAN'T EVEN
LOOK AT ME, CAN YOU?

309
00:14:10,725 --> 00:14:11,850
NOPE.

310
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:14,354
HEY,
IT'S PHOEBE!

311
00:14:14,395 --> 00:14:16,230
WE CAN TALK TO PHOEBE!

312
00:14:17,482 --> 00:14:20,067
NO. I'M TOO
DEPRESSED TO TALK.

313
00:14:20,109 --> 00:14:22,737
I'LL GIVE YOU $1,000
TO TALK TO US.

314
00:14:23,738 --> 00:14:25,532
HEY, YOU GUYS,
WHAT DO YOU THINK

315
00:14:25,573 --> 00:14:28,201
ABOUT MAKING THAT BEACH TRIP
AN ANNUAL THING?

316
00:14:28,242 --> 00:14:30,203
NO!
NO!
NO!

317
00:14:30,244 --> 00:14:32,330
ALL RIGHT,
WHAT HAPPENED
OUT THERE?

318
00:14:32,372 --> 00:14:33,540
WHAT?

319
00:14:33,581 --> 00:14:34,541
WE TOOK A WALK.

320
00:14:34,582 --> 00:14:35,834
NOTHING HAPPENED.

321
00:14:35,875 --> 00:14:38,545
AND I CAME BACK
WITH NOTHING ALL OVER ME.

322
00:14:38,586 --> 00:14:40,505
COME ON, WHAT HAPPENED?

323
00:14:40,547 --> 00:14:41,548
JOEY?

324
00:14:42,882 --> 00:14:44,342
ALL RIGHT.
NO!

325
00:14:44,384 --> 00:14:46,302
JOEY, WE SWORE
WE'D NEVER TELL.

326
00:14:46,344 --> 00:14:48,137
THEY'LL NEVER UNDERSTAND.

327
00:14:50,765 --> 00:14:52,975
WELL, WE HAVE
TO SAY SOMETHING.

328
00:14:53,017 --> 00:14:54,477
WE HAVE TO GET IT OUT.

329
00:14:54,519 --> 00:14:55,854
IT'S EATING ME ALIVE!

330
00:14:57,438 --> 00:15:00,567
MONICA GOT STUNG
BY A JELLYFISH.

331
00:15:00,608 --> 00:15:01,776
ALL RIGHT!

332
00:15:05,029 --> 00:15:07,031
ALL RIGHT.

333
00:15:09,492 --> 00:15:11,494
I GOT STUNG.

334
00:15:12,579 --> 00:15:14,581
STUNG BAD.

335
00:15:16,290 --> 00:15:17,584
I COULDN'T STAND.

336
00:15:17,625 --> 00:15:20,587
I... I COULDN'T WALK.

337
00:15:20,628 --> 00:15:24,257
WE WERE TWO MILES
FROM THE HOUSE.

338
00:15:24,298 --> 00:15:27,260
WE WERE SCARED AND ALONE.

339
00:15:27,301 --> 00:15:29,679
WE DIDN'T THINK
WE COULD MAKE IT.

340
00:15:34,267 --> 00:15:35,935
I WAS IN TOO MUCH PAIN.

341
00:15:35,976 --> 00:15:38,312
AND I WAS TIRED
FROM DIGGING THE HUGE HOLE.

342
00:15:40,565 --> 00:15:44,068
AND THEN, JOEY
REMEMBERED SOMETHING.

343
00:15:44,110 --> 00:15:46,696
I'D SEEN THIS THING
ON THE DISCOVERY CHANNEL.

344
00:15:46,738 --> 00:15:47,697
WAIT A MINUTE.

345
00:15:47,739 --> 00:15:48,698
I SAW THAT.

346
00:15:48,740 --> 00:15:50,366
ON THE DISCOVERY CHANNEL.

347
00:15:50,408 --> 00:15:53,453
YEAH, ABOUT JELLYFISH,
AND HOW IF YOU...

348
00:15:55,580 --> 00:15:57,248
EWW!

349
00:15:57,290 --> 00:15:59,584
YOU PEED
ON YOURSELF?

350
00:15:59,626 --> 00:16:01,586
EWW!
EWW!

351
00:16:01,628 --> 00:16:02,837
YOU CAN'T SAY THAT!

352
00:16:02,879 --> 00:16:04,338
YOU DON'T KNOW!

353
00:16:04,380 --> 00:16:07,759
I MEAN, I THOUGHT
I WOULD PASS OUT
FROM THE PAIN.

354
00:16:07,801 --> 00:16:09,594
ANYWAY, I TRIED...

355
00:16:09,636 --> 00:16:13,180
BUT I COULDN'T...
BEND THAT WAY.

356
00:16:15,057 --> 00:16:16,392
SO...

357
00:16:18,060 --> 00:16:21,063
EWW!
EWW!
EWW!

358
00:16:22,941 --> 00:16:26,402
THAT'S RIGHT, I STEPPED UP!

359
00:16:28,279 --> 00:16:30,531
SHE'S MY FRIEND,
AND SHE NEEDED HELP.

360
00:16:30,573 --> 00:16:34,118
IF I HAD TO,
I'D PEE ON ANY ONE OF YOU.

361
00:16:39,373 --> 00:16:40,792
ONLY, UH...

362
00:16:40,834 --> 00:16:42,042
I COULDN'T.

363
00:16:45,505 --> 00:16:47,507
I GOT THE STAGE FRIGHT.

364
00:16:49,383 --> 00:16:50,343
I WANTED TO HELP

365
00:16:50,384 --> 00:16:51,427
BUT THERE WAS JUST
TOO MUCH PRESSURE

366
00:16:51,469 --> 00:16:54,305
SO... SO I, UH...
I TURNED TO CHANDLER.

367
00:16:54,347 --> 00:16:55,890
( muffled scream )

368
00:16:58,309 --> 00:16:59,853
JOEY KEPT SCREAMING AT ME

369
00:16:59,894 --> 00:17:01,771
"DO IT NOW!
DO IT! DO IT!

370
00:17:01,813 --> 00:17:03,648
DO IT NOW!"

371
00:17:03,690 --> 00:17:05,274
SOMETIMES, LATE AT NIGHT

372
00:17:05,316 --> 00:17:07,443
I CAN STILL HEAR
THE SCREAMING.

373
00:17:09,069 --> 00:17:10,780
( chuckling )

374
00:17:10,822 --> 00:17:12,281
THAT'S 'CAUSE SOMETIMES

375
00:17:12,323 --> 00:17:15,284
I JUST DO IT THROUGH MY WALL
TO FREAK YOU OUT.

376
00:17:15,326 --> 00:17:18,287
Phoebe:
♪ ...AND FUCHSIA AND MAUVE ♪

377
00:17:18,329 --> 00:17:24,711
♪ THOSE ARE THE 66 COLORS
OF MY BEDROOM. ♪

378
00:17:24,752 --> 00:17:25,837
( sparse applause )

379
00:17:25,879 --> 00:17:27,171
THANK YOU.
THANK YOU.

380
00:17:27,213 --> 00:17:29,007
OH, AND I INVITE ALL OF YOU

381
00:17:29,048 --> 00:17:31,968
TO COUNT THE COLORS IN
YOURBEDROOM.

382
00:17:32,010 --> 00:17:33,344
EXCEPT FOR YOU.

383
00:17:33,386 --> 00:17:34,637
YOU GO AWAY.

384
00:17:38,933 --> 00:17:40,434
I'LL GO IN A SECOND.

385
00:17:40,476 --> 00:17:42,269
I JUST WANT TO TELL YOU

386
00:17:42,311 --> 00:17:44,271
THAT THERE
HASN'T BEEN A DAY

387
00:17:44,313 --> 00:17:47,525
WHEN I DIDN'T REGRET
GIVING YOU UP.

388
00:17:47,567 --> 00:17:49,777
OKAY. BYE.

389
00:17:49,819 --> 00:17:51,111
NO. I'M NOT DONE.

390
00:17:51,153 --> 00:17:52,780
I JUST WANT YOU TO KNOW

391
00:17:52,822 --> 00:17:55,783
THAT THE REASON I NEVER
LOOKED YOU UP WAS BECAUSE...

392
00:17:55,825 --> 00:17:58,285
WELL, I WAS AFRAID
THAT YOU WOULD REACT...

393
00:17:58,327 --> 00:18:01,915
JUST, WELL, LIKE THE WAY
YOU'RE REACTING RIGHT NOW

394
00:18:01,956 --> 00:18:03,290
AND... CAN'T WE JUST

395
00:18:03,332 --> 00:18:05,668
YOU KNOW, START
FROM HERE, PLEASE?

396
00:18:07,253 --> 00:18:08,337
NO.

397
00:18:11,549 --> 00:18:13,927
OKAY.

398
00:18:13,968 --> 00:18:15,344
SORRY.

399
00:18:17,430 --> 00:18:19,348
BUT JUST ONE LAST THING.

400
00:18:20,474 --> 00:18:23,061
YOU KNOW, YOU CAME
LOOKING FOR FAMILY.

401
00:18:24,353 --> 00:18:26,146
I'M FAMILY.

402
00:18:26,188 --> 00:18:27,231
( sighs )

403
00:18:27,273 --> 00:18:28,357
I'M IT.

404
00:18:32,028 --> 00:18:34,030
WELL, NOW I'M DONE.

405
00:18:36,365 --> 00:18:40,202
BUT IT'S NOT LIKE WE'RE
LOSING ANYTHING, YOU KNOW?

406
00:18:40,244 --> 00:18:43,456
YEAH, I GUESS YOU'RE RIGHT.

407
00:18:43,497 --> 00:18:46,125
IT'S NOT LIKE WE KNOW
EACH OTHER OR ANYTHING

408
00:18:46,166 --> 00:18:48,002
OR THAT WE HAVE
ANYTHING IN COMMON.

409
00:18:48,044 --> 00:18:49,169
WELL, I DON'T KNOW.

410
00:18:49,211 --> 00:18:50,504
I MEAN, IT'S NOT LIKE

411
00:18:50,546 --> 00:18:52,632
WE DON'T HAVE
ANYTHING IN COMMON.

412
00:18:54,842 --> 00:18:57,344
I MEAN, I LIKE PIZZA.

413
00:18:57,386 --> 00:18:59,764
I... I LIKE PIZZA.

414
00:18:59,806 --> 00:19:01,348
YOU DO! HA!

415
00:19:01,390 --> 00:19:04,268
WAIT, I LIKE, UM, THE BEATLES.

416
00:19:04,310 --> 00:19:05,979
OH, MY GOD, SO DO I!

417
00:19:06,020 --> 00:19:06,854
OH, I KNEW IT!

418
00:19:06,896 --> 00:19:07,855
WOW!

419
00:19:07,897 --> 00:19:08,856
WAIT-WAIT-WAIT.

420
00:19:08,898 --> 00:19:10,190
PUPPIES-- CUTE OR UGLY?

421
00:19:10,232 --> 00:19:11,317
OH, SO CUTE.

422
00:19:11,358 --> 00:19:12,401
UH-HUH! WELL?

423
00:19:12,443 --> 00:19:15,321
YOU SEE?

424
00:19:15,362 --> 00:19:17,991
BUT I'M STILL... I'M MAD AT YOU.

425
00:19:18,032 --> 00:19:19,325
I KNOW.

426
00:19:20,576 --> 00:19:23,162
I'M MAD AT ME, TOO.

427
00:19:23,203 --> 00:19:26,124
WELL, UM, DO YOU WANT
TO GET SOMETHING TO EAT?

428
00:19:26,165 --> 00:19:28,542
'CAUSE I'M
KIND OF HUNGRY.

429
00:19:28,584 --> 00:19:30,628
HEY! ME, TOO!

430
00:19:30,670 --> 00:19:32,212
STOP IT.
NOW YOU'RE JUST DOING IT

431
00:19:32,254 --> 00:19:34,090
TO FREAK ME OUT.

432
00:19:38,761 --> 00:19:40,054
( deep sigh )

433
00:19:40,096 --> 00:19:42,264
OH, I MISSED YOU.

434
00:19:42,306 --> 00:19:44,266
I MISSED YOU, TOO.

435
00:19:46,894 --> 00:19:49,897
OH, I WAS SO NERVOUS
ABOUT THAT LETTER.

436
00:19:52,399 --> 00:19:55,153
BUT THE WAY YOU
OWNED UP TO EVERYTHING

437
00:19:55,194 --> 00:19:57,030
IT JUST... SHOWED ME

438
00:19:57,071 --> 00:19:59,657
HOW MUCH YOU'VE
GROWN, YOU KNOW?

439
00:20:02,242 --> 00:20:03,953
I SUPPOSE.

440
00:20:03,995 --> 00:20:06,664
NO, YOU HAVE,
ROSS, YOU HAVE.

441
00:20:06,706 --> 00:20:09,000
YOU SHOULD GIVE
YOURSELF CREDIT.

442
00:20:09,042 --> 00:20:12,294
I MEAN, MY MOM NEVERTHOUGHT
THIS WOULD WORK OUT.

443
00:20:12,336 --> 00:20:13,754
( chuckling )

444
00:20:13,796 --> 00:20:16,799
SHE WAS ALL,
"ONCE A CHEATER,
ALWAYS A CHEATER."

445
00:20:18,968 --> 00:20:20,469
MM-HMM.

446
00:20:20,511 --> 00:20:24,431
OH... I JUST WISH
WE HADN'T LOST
THOSE FOUR MONTHS.

447
00:20:24,473 --> 00:20:26,934
BUT IF TIME WAS
WHAT YOU NEEDED

448
00:20:26,976 --> 00:20:31,689
JUST TO GAIN A
LITTLE PERSPECTIVE...

449
00:20:31,731 --> 00:20:34,608
Ross:
WE WERE
ON A BREAK!

450
00:20:34,650 --> 00:20:36,360
COFFEE HOUSE?

451
00:20:36,402 --> 00:20:38,071
YOU BET.

452
00:20:38,112 --> 00:20:40,781
AND FOR THE RECORD,
IT TOOK TWO PEOPLE

453
00:20:40,823 --> 00:20:43,076
TO BREAK UP
THIS RELATIONSHIP.

454
00:20:43,117 --> 00:20:45,078
YOU AND THAT GIRL
FROM THE COPY PLACE

455
00:20:45,119 --> 00:20:47,663
WHICH, YESTERDAY, YOU TOOK
FULL RESPONSIBILITY FOR.

456
00:20:47,705 --> 00:20:50,958
I DIDN'T KNOW WHAT I WAS
TAKING RESPONSIBILITY FOR, OKAY?

457
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:52,710
I DIDN'T FINISH
THE WHOLE LETTER.

458
00:20:52,752 --> 00:20:53,335
WHAT?

459
00:20:53,377 --> 00:20:54,879
I FELL ASLEEP.

460
00:20:54,921 --> 00:20:57,798
YOU FELL ASLEEP?

461
00:20:57,840 --> 00:21:00,634
IT WAS 5:30 IN THE MORNING

462
00:21:00,676 --> 00:21:05,639
AND YOU HAD RAMBLED ON
FOR 18 PAGES.

463
00:21:07,225 --> 00:21:09,560
FRONT AND BACK!

464
00:21:09,602 --> 00:21:10,728
( groans )

465
00:21:10,770 --> 00:21:12,521
OH-OH-OH, AND BY THE WAY

466
00:21:12,563 --> 00:21:14,857
Y-O-U APOSTROPHE R-E

467
00:21:14,899 --> 00:21:16,316
MEANS "YOU ARE."

468
00:21:16,358 --> 00:21:18,194
Y-O-U-R MEANS "YOUR."

469
00:21:18,236 --> 00:21:19,820
HA! YOU KNOW,
I CAN'T BELIEVE

470
00:21:19,862 --> 00:21:22,698
I EVEN THOUGHT OF GETTING
BACK TOGETHER WITH YOU.

471
00:21:22,740 --> 00:21:24,158
WE ARE SO OVER.

472
00:21:24,200 --> 00:21:25,993
( choked up ):
OH... OH... OH...

473
00:21:26,035 --> 00:21:27,327
FINE BY ME!

474
00:21:27,369 --> 00:21:31,249
OH, AND HEY, THOSE
LITTLE SPELLING TIPS

475
00:21:31,290 --> 00:21:32,291
WILL COME IN HANDY

476
00:21:32,332 --> 00:21:33,167
WHEN YOU'RE AT HOME
ON SATURDAY NIGHTS

477
00:21:33,209 --> 00:21:34,877
PLAYING SCRABBLE
WITH MONICA!

478
00:21:34,919 --> 00:21:36,545
HEY...
SORRY!

479
00:21:36,587 --> 00:21:39,423
I JUST FEEL BAD
ABOUT ALL THAT SLEEP
YOU'RE GOING TO MISS

480
00:21:39,465 --> 00:21:41,050
WISHING YOU
WERE WITH ME.

481
00:21:41,092 --> 00:21:44,095
OH, NO-NO-NO, DON'T YOU WORRY
ABOUT ME FALLING ASLEEP.

482
00:21:44,137 --> 00:21:46,806
I STILL HAVE YOUR LETTER!

483
00:21:46,847 --> 00:21:50,059
AND HEY, JUST SO YOU KNOW...

484
00:21:50,101 --> 00:21:51,393
IT'S NOT THAT COMMON

485
00:21:51,435 --> 00:21:53,479
IT DOESN'T HAPPEN TO EVERY GUY

486
00:21:53,520 --> 00:21:55,898
AND IT IS A BIG DEAL!

487
00:21:55,940 --> 00:21:58,358
I KNEW IT!

488
00:22:04,322 --> 00:22:06,284
GIN.

489
00:22:06,325 --> 00:22:10,412
WE WERE PLAYING GIN?

490
00:22:10,454 --> 00:22:11,247
YOU KNOW,
IF WE WERE A COUPLE

491
00:22:11,289 --> 00:22:12,748
WE COULD PLAY THIS GAME NAKED.

492
00:22:12,790 --> 00:22:14,416
( laughing )

493
00:22:14,458 --> 00:22:16,169
WOULD YOU STOP?

494
00:22:16,210 --> 00:22:18,171
OKAY. ALL RIGHT.

495
00:22:18,212 --> 00:22:19,297
OKAY, ALL RIGHT.

496
00:22:19,338 --> 00:22:21,090
I THINK YOU'RE GREAT.

497
00:22:21,132 --> 00:22:24,302
I THINK YOU'RE SWEET
AND YOU'RE SMART

498
00:22:24,342 --> 00:22:25,928
AND I LOVE YOU.

499
00:22:25,970 --> 00:22:29,765
BUT YOU WILL
ALWAYS BE THE GUY
WHO PEED ON ME.

500
00:22:29,807 --> 00:22:32,101
[Captioned by
The Caption Center
WGBH Educational Foundation]

